    <briefdescription>
<para>Generic helpers (<computeroutput><ref refid="mat-util_8hpp_a1109fbe3c04d038304324bcb8a66d8c4_1a1109fbe3c04d038304324bcb8a66d8c4" kindref="member">displayMat</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-util_8hpp_a74cc79c6ebb813de1ea8c131ada987ca_1a74cc79c6ebb813de1ea8c131ada987ca" kindref="member">concatenateMatrices</ref></computeroutput>) for <computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_mat" kindref="compound">DMat</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_mat" kindref="compound">SMat</ref></computeroutput> matrices. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Collects the templated utilities that do not fit naturally into <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-arith_8hpp" kindref="compound">mat-arith.hpp</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-elem-ops_8hpp" kindref="compound">mat-elem-ops.hpp</ref></computeroutput>, or <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-linalg_8hpp" kindref="compound">mat-linalg.hpp</ref></computeroutput>. <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-util_8hpp_a1109fbe3c04d038304324bcb8a66d8c4_1a1109fbe3c04d038304324bcb8a66d8c4" kindref="member">displayMat</ref>&lt;Mat&gt;(<ref refid="classbuffer" kindref="compound">buffer</ref>&amp; o, const Mat&amp; A)</computeroutput> walks any duck-typed <computeroutput>Mat</computeroutput> exposing <computeroutput>ElementType</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>ring()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>numRows()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>numColumns()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>entry(r, c)</computeroutput>, builds one per-row sub-buffer, pads each column to the widest entry, marks zero entries with <computeroutput>.</computeroutput>, and emits the assembled rows through the <computeroutput><ref refid="classbuffer" kindref="compound">buffer</ref></computeroutput> followed by <computeroutput><ref refid="m2-types_8cpp_a9652bd683300dd969acdf07396e1c1dd_1a9652bd683300dd969acdf07396e1c1dd" kindref="member">newline</ref></computeroutput>. The one-argument overload <computeroutput>displayMat(A)</computeroutput> wraps the same routine and flushes via <computeroutput><ref refid="text-io_8cpp_a5bd0b57b7653fb12e1dcaa8c4d09ce4e_1a5bd0b57b7653fb12e1dcaa8c4d09ce4e" kindref="member">emit</ref></computeroutput> from <computeroutput><ref refid="text-io_8hpp" kindref="compound">text-io.hpp</ref></computeroutput>. Both <computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_mat" kindref="compound">DMat</ref>&lt;R&gt;</computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_s_mat" kindref="compound">SMat</ref>&lt;R&gt;</computeroutput> satisfy the contract.</para>
<para>The companion <computeroutput><ref refid="mat-util_8hpp_a74cc79c6ebb813de1ea8c131ada987ca_1a74cc79c6ebb813de1ea8c131ada987ca" kindref="member">concatenateMatrices</ref>&lt;Mat&gt;(A, B, C)</computeroutput> writes the horizontal join <computeroutput>[A | B]</computeroutput> into a caller-supplied <computeroutput>C</computeroutput> (after resizing it to <computeroutput>A.numRows() <ref refid="overflow-test_8cpp_aa07f992d22249e2bef61db62f71671b2_1aa07f992d22249e2bef61db62f71671b2" kindref="member">x</ref> (A.numColumns() + B.numColumns())</computeroutput>), asserting that <computeroutput>A</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>B</computeroutput> have the same row count.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="buffer_8hpp" kindref="compound">buffer.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="text-io_8hpp" kindref="compound">text-io.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="dmat_8hpp" kindref="compound">dmat.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="smat_8hpp" kindref="compound">smat.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
